glob:COR-1: The twelve `COR-N` tables define twelve corridors of rooms that have sight-lines to each other. (Some of the “corridors” are outdoors.) Each room in a corridor has that bit set in its [prop:CORRIDOR] property.
	This permits the game to display messages like “Mrs. Robner, off to the north, ducks into a room to the north.”

prop:CORRIDOR: This property defines one or more “corridors” (sight-lines) that the player can see down from a given room. See [glob:COR-1].



rtn:V-ZORK: The `ZORK` command was removed from the grammar early on; no known release recognizes it. This vestige remains.

obj:STAIRS: This room lists itself as a scenery object (the `GLOBAL` property). This doesn’t seem to have any effect, but it doesn’t hurt the game either. It threw my Visible Zorker code for a loop though!

